SCOPE
-----
This license applies to the Otzaria Ashurit and Otzaria Ashurit Nikud
typefaces — the font source files in this repository, the compiled font
files built from them, the build scripts, and any other content of this
repository not stated to be otherwise licensed.

This license does NOT apply to third-party tools used to build the fonts
(Python, fontTools, skia-pathops, Pillow and other dependencies). Those
remain subject to their own respective licenses.


1. Personal Use Permission
Permission is granted to an individual natural person to download,
install, use, study, and modify the covered fonts solely for that
person's own private, personal, and non-commercial use — including
setting and printing documents for that person's own use.

2. No Public Use
Without prior express written permission from the copyright holder, you
may not use the covered fonts, or any modified or derivative version of
them, in any product, project, service, platform, website, application,
plugin, library, API, bot, database, document, publication, or other
system that is made available to, distributed to, or used for the
benefit of any third party or members of the public.

This restriction applies whether the public use is commercial,
non-commercial, charitable, educational, open-source, freeware, paid, or
provided without charge.

3. Otzaria Exception
Notwithstanding sections 2, 4, 5 and 6, the Otzaria Project may bundle,
embed, distribute, and display the covered fonts as an integral part of
the Otzaria application (otzaria.org) and its installers and packages,
on any platform, and may embed them in files that the application
produces for its users, such as exported or printed PDF documents.

A person who receives the covered fonts this way — as part of the
Otzaria application — may use them within that application, and may use
documents the application produced with them, without any further
permission. That person receives no right to extract, copy, install,
redistribute, or otherwise use the fonts outside the Otzaria
application; for any such use, sections 1, 2 and 4 through 8
apply in full.

This exception is granted to the Otzaria Project alone. It does not
extend to any fork, derivative, repackaging, or redistribution of the
Otzaria application by any other person or entity.

4. No Distribution
You may not copy, publish, redistribute, sublicense, sell, lend,
transfer, upload, mirror, or otherwise make the covered fonts, their
source files, compiled versions, modified versions, or derivative works
available to any other person or entity.

5. No Organizational Use
No company, organization, association, institution, nonprofit, charity,
educational institution, government body, community, or other legal
entity may use the covered fonts — including for internal purposes —
without prior express written permission from the copyright holder.

6. No Embedding or Bundling
You may not embed the covered fonts in, or bundle them with, any
software, application, document, electronic publication, or file that is
distributed or made available to any other person or entity. Embedding
in a document that remains in your own private use is permitted.

7. Private Modifications
You may create modifications solely for your own permitted personal use.
You may not publish, distribute, contribute, submit, or make those
modifications available to others without prior express written
permission.

8. Attribution
Any permitted use, copy, modification, or derivative work of the covered
fonts — including ingestion, training, processing, or reuse by language
models (LLMs) or any other automated system — requires clear credit to
the Otzaria Project (otzaria.org).

This attribution is an integral part of the license terms, and the
obligation to give credit remains in force even after a separate
